# Vivaha Studio project context

## Scope and status

Mobile-first wedding invitations with emotional, elegant bespoke designs. Free Beta ships source for Royal Rajputana (`royal`), Floral Elegance (`floral-elegance`) and Royal 3D Wedding Cinema (`royal-3d-cinema`). Owners browse, preview, create, edit details/media/events, publish and share. The cap is three total invitations, including published ones. RSVP is WhatsApp/external link; there are no payments, guest records, tracking or analytics. Do not promise unlimited creation, unavailable templates, bespoke services or unsupported customer/rating/adoption evidence. Illustrative examples are labelled accordingly.

Tasks 01–15 and task 16 readiness assessment are complete with recorded limits; the user-authorized matching Production release is live. See [current evidence](../../docs/task-16-verification.md) for local/live passes and unresolved browser/device/deployment gates. Follow [root operating memory](../../AGENTS.md) and [roadmap](../../docs/next-steps-prompts.md). The user authorized Supabase migrations and disposable provider testing on the shared local/production setup. Five migrations, preserved original rows/backfill, one-owner REST lifecycle/quota and generated PNG/WAV signing/upload/completion now pass. Exact original counts are 5 invitations, 3 published; do not use table-list estimates as evidence of emptiness. Generated fixtures were removed. The five-case two-owner database suite now passes, including isolation and RLS-hidden collisions. 40 distinct authenticated Chrome/WebKit browser cases pass; PR #20 is merged; matching Production is live; real devices/WhatsApp and real-user Auth remain human checks. Commit/push and Vercel Preview configuration are authorized; The user subsequently accepted the Preview and authorized production configuration, merging PR #20 and deployment; personal-data deletion remains unauthorized. Do not claim production readiness from partial passes.

## Stack and source ownership

Next.js 16.3.8 App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind, Zustand, Supabase Auth/PostgreSQL, Cloudinary, Framer Motion, installed Radix primitives, react-easy-crop and Sonner. CI uses Node 22/npm. Keep code readable, practical and mobile-first; avoid unnecessary abstractions/dependencies and excessive effects. Persist wedding data separately from preview/crop/navigation UI state. No business/data fetching logic inside templates.

| Source | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `src/app` | Marketing/auth/owner/public routes, upload API boundaries |
| `src/features/invitations` | Owner editor, write coordination, navigation, publication/share actions |
| `src/features/dashboard` | Editing panels and marketing sections/cards |
| `src/stores/invitation-editor-store.ts` | Working editor content and local/acknowledged versions |
| `src/lib` | Normalization, readiness, links/share images, origin/media/maps/auth helpers |
| `src/templates` | Metadata, SSR-enabled lazy runtime registry, presentation-only designs |
