| `docs`, `tests/e2e`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | Contracts, pending verification and existing smoke infrastructure |

AuthProvider is the single client auth source for navigation. DashboardShell/NavChrome controls marketing chrome; the invitation editor supplies its own header/back/status/step actions. Mobile auth/account lives in the Studio bottom menu, with the top profile dropdown on desktop. Preserve existing design identity and contact details.

## Storage, authorization and publication

Nested WeddingData remains JSONB. `profiles` stores auth-linked owner identity. `invitations` stores private working content even while published; owner SELECT/DELETE only after final migrations. `published_invitations` stores a frozen public copy with anonymous/authenticated SELECT only. Never hide private columns in UI on an otherwise public row; table/view/RPC grants and RLS define the boundary.

Creation uses `create_invitation_draft`, infers auth owner and serializes on the owner's profile before counting all invitations. No direct table/column INSERT or alternate bypass. Existing above-cap owners keep their rows.

Save/publish/unpublish use owner-authorized, row-locked, expected-revision RPCs; direct UPDATE/public-copy writes are revoked. Autosave updates working content only. Publish atomically promotes the saved row; public page and metadata share the same request-cached snapshot read. Owner routes/preview read private content. Unpublish deletes public access without losing working content/history. See [database](../../supabase-db.md), [persistence](../../docs/invitation-persistence.md) and [quota](../../docs/invitation-quota.md).

The editor has one ordered write pipeline. Debounce reads latest store content when work runs. Publication cancels/drains queued saves and sends the intended saved revision; responses merge lifecycle metadata without replacing newer local fields. New edits during a dispatched publish remain private until a later republish. Invitation change/unmount invalidates old session acknowledgements; errors unlock controls, retain edits and provide retry. A timeout can occur after commit: reconcile authoritative state, not guessed revisions.

Creation reserves a generated unique slug; first publication allocates readable names with unique-constraint arbitration and bounded suffix retries, including RLS-hidden collisions. Thereafter exact slug/suffix survives name edits, republish and unpublish/re-publish. No rename feature/preflight-only collision logic. Copy/display/share use the persisted slug and canonical origin.

## Editor safety and readiness

Unsaved changes, in-flight saves and errors protect internal navigation, Back/Forward and reload/close; beforeunload alone is insufficient. Save/discard/cancel uses the same queue. Save failure does not navigate or claim success. Owner/invitation-scoped device recovery is best effort, expires after seven days, handles stale server revisions explicitly and clears on discard/sign-out as appropriate. Discard cannot undo an already-sent transaction.

Shared TypeScript validation and the database publish transaction require real couple names, valid wedding day, usable event/main venue and RSVP destination when enabled. Optional story/photos remain optional. Starter/demo content requires guidance/acknowledgement; existing optional omissions do not block republish. Media/map/external RSVP URLs reject unsafe protocols, credentials and malformed inputs through validation/safe rendering without destroying accepted legacy JSONB. Draft autosave accepts partial forms. See [editor contract](../../docs/editor-safety.md).

## Media and sharing

Authenticated JSON signing/completion endpoints never forward file bytes through Next. Browser sends cropped images/audio directly to Cloudinary; server confirms owner-bound asset type/format/actual bytes before attachment. Use owner-scoped folders, signed presets and server-only keys; cancellation/timeout/unmount retains prior URLs and ignores late responses. 8/12 MiB image/audio attachment limits do not imply pre-storage provider byte limits. Admin reads, signed presets and fixed-folder operation are confirmed with generated fixtures. Account ceilings/cost/rate operations and deployed CORS/CSP remain separate review items. See [upload contract](../../docs/cloudinary-uploads.md).

One share resolver uses explicit OG image → explicit WhatsApp image → hero → no image, preserves explicit choices and existing crops, and applies the final Cloudinary 1200×630 share transform. Owner preview describes the next publication; public metadata stays frozen. WhatsApp caches can lag republishing. NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL must be explicitly configured for browser/server production agreement; VERCEL_URL alone is server-only. See [sharing/loading](../../docs/sharing-and-template-loading.md).

## Template architecture and mobile behavior

Registry metadata is the single source of IDs/names/thumbnails/categories/descriptions. Marketing derives from it without importing template components. Runtime registry declares selected SSR-enabled Next dynamic loaders; never switch all guest content to client-only loading. TemplateId derives from metadata; garden-mandap maps centrally to royal-3d-cinema. Bespoke sections share WeddingData contracts and preview IDs. Future template work is outside this roadmap and must coordinate loader/metadata/database allowlists. See [template architecture](template-architecture.mdc).

Radix ModalSurface/shared Dialog owns focus containment/restoration, background isolation, scroll locking and nested Escape. Template overlays stay inline to inherit their palette/zoom. Use native/accessibly managed selects, coherent labels/errors and local gallery key handlers; preserve drag and touch behavior. See [overlay contract](../../docs/accessible-overlays.md).

Prefer mobile layouts and at least 44px targets, including zoom-scaled invitations; shared form text is 16px on mobile. Keep long names/errors within preview widths and sticky controls usable with keyboards/safe areas. Reduced motion has static decorative/poster alternatives, real pause/play for the illustrative marquee, immediate interaction-based opening, and preserved skip/reveal/tap-first music. Studio theme must not change template/on-image contrast. Demo calendar uses one caller-supplied server/creation reference +90 days, serialized for hydration; never advance saved real dates. Explicit timezone labels avoid host differences. See [polish contract](../../docs/mobile-motion-theme-and-demos.md).

## Session routes, immutable assets and cleanup

Only explicit static namespaces/exact files bypass Supabase refresh; protected `/dashboard` root/slash descendants remain protected despite media-like segments/file extensions. Auth callbacks, safe redirects/recovery and upload authorization remain separate. Preserve versioned cache/range serving. See [routing/copy](../../docs/session-routing-and-product-copy.md).

Confirmed unused components/dependencies/starter SVGs were removed. Keep framer-motion/radix-ui, active upload/openers/scratch date components, coordinate schema/maps, all templates, migrations/tests/docs/.env.example. Keep dynamic frames, active posters/decor/music and immutable Royal 3D v1/archive manifest positions/validator requirements. Legacy tap-to-open media and cold v1 assets need historical-deployment/saved-content evidence before retirement. See [cleanup inventory](../../docs/cleanup-decisions.md).

